<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI23-BLOCK-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI23-BLOCK-004" ;
  triage:title "RULE-003 file-size violation in crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs" ;
  triage:description "Global file size exceeds 1000-line non-test-code decomposition limit. crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs non-test code spans lines 1-1022 (the #[cfg(test)] module begins at line 1023), exceeding the 1000-line limit. This violates RULE-003 zero-tolerance architecture file-size constraint. Suggested remediation: split runtime_health.rs into submodules under crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/ (e.g. extract doctor-finding construction, dispatcher status/snapshot logic, or the ApiRouter::route match arms). Followup pass (2026-07-26): quality-mgr QA recheck of PR #630 (AI.24, branch feature/pAI-s24-host-qualified-ack-receipt, head 1daef214) independently confirmed via arch-qa that the file is still 1065 non-test lines on that branch, i.e. this pre-existing finding also recurs on the s24 branch (previously recorded occurrences existed only on integrate/phase-AI, s27, s28, s29, s30). The AI.24->AI.25 forward merge already landed, so s25 carries an identical violation. A sweep of s26 (not yet mentioned by quality-mgr) also found the file still over the limit." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
